Kubernetes Project – Troubleshooting Commands with Explanations
1. Check Container Runtime
sudo systemctl status containerd
(Checks whether the containerd container runtime is active and running.)
2. Check Kubernetes Nodes
kubectl get nodes -o wide
(Displays all Kubernetes nodes, their status, IP addresses, roles and Kubernetes versions.)
3. Check Kubernetes System Pods
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -o wide
(Checks Kubernetes system components such as CoreDNS, kube-proxy and Calico.)
4. Check Calico Network Interface
ip -d link show tunl0
(Checks the Calico IP-in-IP tunnel interface and its network configuration.)
5. Check Kubernetes API Server Connectivity
curl -k --connect-timeout 5 https://172.31.24.71:6443/version
(Tests connectivity to the Kubernetes API server running on the master node. The -k option skips certificate verification for this connectivity test.)
6. Check DNS Resolution from Master
kubectl exec dns-master-test -- nslookup kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local 10.96.0.10
(Tests DNS resolution through the CoreDNS Kubernetes Service IP from a pod on the master.)
kubectl exec dns-master-test -- nslookup kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local 192.168.235.196
(Tests DNS resolution directly through a CoreDNS pod IP.)
7. Check DNS Resolution from Worker
kubectl exec dns-worker-test -- nslookup kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local 192.168.235.196
(Tests whether a worker-node pod can communicate with the CoreDNS pod on the master.)
kubectl exec dns-worker-test -- nslookup kubernetes.default.svc.cluster.local 10.96.0.10
(Tests DNS resolution through the CoreDNS Service IP from the worker.)
8. Check Kubernetes Service Connectivity
kubectl exec net-test -- curl -k -v --connect-timeout 5 https://10.96.0.1:443/version
(Tests connectivity from a pod to the Kubernetes API Service IP.)
9. Check Calico Networking
kubectl get pods -n calico-system -o wide
(Checks Calico networking pods and identifies which nodes they are running on.)
kubectl get ippools.crd.projectcalico.org
(Displays Calico IP pools configured for pod networking.)
10. Check GitHub Repository Branch
git ls-remote --heads https://github.com/psreddy2508/DevOps-Project-Zomato-Kastro.git
(Checks the remote GitHub repository branches and identifies the correct branch. We confirmed that the branch is master.)
11. Clone GitHub Repository
git clone https://github.com/psreddy2508/DevOps-Project-Zomato-Kastro.git /tmp/zomato-check
(Downloads the Zomato project repository to the master node for inspecting Kubernetes manifests.)
12. Inspect Kubernetes YAML Files
cat /tmp/zomato-check/Kubernetes/deployment.yaml
(Displays the Zomato Deployment manifest.)
cat /tmp/zomato-check/Kubernetes/service.yaml
(Displays the Zomato Service manifest.)
cat /tmp/zomato-check/Kubernetes/node-service.yaml
(Displays the Node Exporter Service manifest that caused the Argo CD synchronization error.)
13. Identify Node Exporter Configuration
grep -RniE 'node-exporter|prometheus-node-exporter' /tmp/zomato-check/Kubernetes/
(Searches all files under the Kubernetes directory for Node Exporter references.)
14. Remove Unwanted Node Exporter Manifest
cd /tmp/zomato-check
(Changes the working directory to the cloned project.)
rm -f Kubernetes/node-service.yaml
(Removes the Node Exporter Service YAML file from the local repository because monitoring is not part of the current project.)
15. Check Argo CD Application
kubectl get applications -n argocd
(Displays Argo CD applications and their synchronization and health status.)
kubectl describe application zomato -n argocd
(Displays detailed information about the Zomato Argo CD application, including Git revision, sync errors and managed resources.)
16. Refresh Argo CD
kubectl annotate application zomato -n argocd argocd.argoproj.io/refresh=hard --overwrite
(Forces Argo CD to refresh its repository information and recalculate application status.)
17. Check Zomato Pods
kubectl get pods -n default -o wide
(Checks Zomato pod status, readiness, restart count, pod IP and worker-node placement.)
18. Check Zomato Service
kubectl get svc zomato -n default
(Checks the Zomato Service type, ClusterIP and NodePort configuration.)
19. Check Argo CD Services
kubectl get svc -n argocd
(Displays Argo CD Services, including argocd-server, which provides dashboard access.)
20. Access Argo CD Dashboard
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443
(Forwards local port 8080 to the Argo CD HTTPS service port 443. Access it locally through https://localhost:8080.)
21. Retrieve Initial Argo CD Password
kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d; echo
(Retrieves and decodes the initial Argo CD admin password, if the initial secret still exists.)

